{
  "id": "COMPOUND:24149 - PROTEIN:5940",
  "verbalization": "Mexogenin appears to interact with Carboxylesterase 2 through a series of intermediate targets, all of which are proteins that are targets of Mexogenin. The evidence suggests that Mexogenin acts as a target for Microtubule-associated protein 1B, which in turn is a target of two other compounds—5-Chloro-2-(2,5-Dihydroxybenzyl)-3-(Hydroxymethyl)Benzene-1,4-Diol and Amurensin. These compounds all ultimately direct their activity to Carboxylesterase 2. The integration of these pathways implies that Mexogenin may influence Carboxylesterase 2 through a network of molecular interactions, potentially modulating its enzymatic activity. The shared involvement of Carboxylesterase 2 across multiple targets suggests a possible functional relationship, though the exact mechanism of interaction remains to be elucidated.",
